+    request; stale values are a compliance issue, SOX control C-14);
+  - ``get_balance`` and ``list_open_invoices`` (``_UNCACHED_OPS``). These
+    were taken out of the cache after reports of cross-tenant leaks whose
+    root cause was never identified. As a side effect, each call to them
+    also clears the *entire* cache, for all tenants.
+
+* Invalidation: every write through the service (``upsert_customer``,
+  ``create_invoice``, ``mark_invoice_paid``) clears the entire cache, for
+  all tenants, straight after the database write. Nothing is invalidated
+  per key or per tenant.
+* Staleness: a cached entry is served while it is younger than
+  ``ttl_seconds`` (default 300 s; ``0`` disables cache hits). Writes that
+  bypass the service, e.g. back-office edits made directly in the database
+  (BILL-2324), are therefore visible after at most ``ttl_seconds``. The same
+  bound applies to writes made through a *different* ``BillingService``
+  instance that does not share this instance's ``Cache``.
+"""
